Deviations from upstream (deliberate)
- deploy: mirror instead of rm -rf; only files from the previous deploy list
  are removed, foreign files stay; a foreign file that must be replaced is
  saved by fsx first. The git-diff incremental branch is gone (payload is not
  a git repo); an unchanged file is simply not rewritten. __pycache__ skipped.
- compositor config dir: upstream deleted every file not in the source; we do
  the same (after the *_backup copy) but keep owned files and files of
  selected modules (user_keybinds.lua).
- bootstrap no longer installs fzf/pciutils (they served the bash UI only).
- cp errors in the compositor backup stop the run (upstream ignored them).
- root file writes go through `sudo install` (whitelisted), not tee/cp/sed.
- core.wallpapers (3 random pictures, a ~300 MiB clone) is opt-in
  (Options.WallpaperSample); the wallpapers module is the full pack.
- no telemetry anywhere.

