Stage 8: how to run and watch the VM stand
- Images live OUTSIDE git: tests/vm/{images,state,out} are symlinks to ~/vmstand/
  (/tmp is a 7.8G tmpfs, qcow2 images would eat RAM).
- Build the base image once (~2 min):   tests/vm/vm.sh base
- Boot an overlay:                      tests/vm/vm.sh up NAME ; tests/vm/vm.sh ssh ; tests/vm/vm.sh down
- WATCH live in a terminal (kitty):     tmux attach -t serp-vm
  (created by `tests/vm/vm.sh watch`, which the scenarios call; window "tui" mirrors the
  tmux session "tui" inside the VM that the TUI scenarios drive; ctrl-b n = serial console log)
- Real QEMU window instead of headless: VM_DISPLAY=gtk tests/vm/vm.sh up NAME   (or sdl)
- Scenarios: tests/vm/scenarios/NN-*.sh (each prints PASS/FAIL, logs in tests/vm/out/NN/).

